_title','Download the report'),(87569,1929,'_report_title','field_62f30edfb57e1'),(87570,1929,'report_intro','Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Phasellus massa erat, consectetur at semper at, feugiat vel orci. '),(87571,1929,'_report_intro','field_62f30eedb57e2'),(87572,1929,'report_link_url','#'),(87573,1929,'_report_link_url','field_62f30ef4b57e3'),(87574,1929,'report_link_text','Download'),(87575,1929,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(87576,1929,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(87577,1929,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(87578,1929,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(87579,1929,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(87580,1929,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(87581,1929,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(87582,1929,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(87583,1929,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(87584,1929,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(87585,1929,'_problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text','field_640fa11a81d97'),(87586,1929,'problem_icons','4