_title','Download the report'),(135031,2264,'_report_title','field_62f30edfb57e1'),(135032,2264,'report_intro','Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Phasellus massa erat, consectetur at semper at, feugiat vel orci. '),(135033,2264,'_report_intro','field_62f30eedb57e2'),(135034,2264,'report_link_url','#'),(135035,2264,'_report_link_url','field_62f30ef4b57e3'),(135036,2264,'report_link_text','Download'),(135037,2264,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(135038,2264,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(135039,2264,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(135040,2264,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(135041,2264,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(135042,2264,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(135043,2264,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(135044,2264,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(135045,2264,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(135046,2264,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(135047,2264,'_problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text','field_640fa11a81d97'),(135048,2264,