03,2672,'_survey_index_7_survey_title','field_6294564042238'),(182204,2672,'survey_index_7_survey_url','#'),(182205,2672,'_survey_index_7_survey_url','field_6294564e42239'),(182206,2672,'survey_index_7_survey_url_text','View Results'),(182207,2672,'_survey_index_7_survey_url_text','field_629456584223a'),(182208,2672,'survey_index','8'),(182209,2672,'_survey_index','field_6294561242236'),(182210,2672,'report_title','Download the report'),(182211,2672,'_report_title','field_62f30edfb57e1'),(182212,2672,'report_intro','Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Phasellus massa erat, consectetur at semper at, feugiat vel orci. '),(182213,2672,'_report_intro','field_62f30eedb57e2'),(182214,2672,'report_link_url','#'),(182215,2672,'_report_link_url','field_62f30ef4b57e3'),(182216,2672,'report_link_text','Download'),(182217,2672,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(182218,2672,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(182219,2672,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(182220,2672,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(182221,2672,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(182222,2672,'problem_ico