3,2740,'report_intro','Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Phasellus massa erat, consectetur at semper at, feugiat vel orci. '),(204914,2740,'_report_intro','field_62f30eedb57e2'),(204915,2740,'report_link_url','#'),(204916,2740,'_report_link_url','field_62f30ef4b57e3'),(204917,2740,'report_link_text','Download'),(204918,2740,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(204919,2740,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(204920,2740,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(204921,2740,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(204922,2740,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(204923,2740,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(204924,2740,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(204925,2740,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(204926,2740,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(204927,2740,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(204928,2740,'_problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text','field_640fa11a81d97'),(204929,2740,'problem_icons','4'),(204930,2740,'_problem_icons','field_640fa0191d518'),(204931,2740,'c