l','field_6294564e42239'),(208725,2763,'survey_index_7_survey_url_text','View Results'),(208726,2763,'_survey_index_7_survey_url_text','field_629456584223a'),(208727,2763,'survey_index','8'),(208728,2763,'_survey_index','field_6294561242236'),(208729,2763,'report_title','Download the report'),(208730,2763,'_report_title','field_62f30edfb57e1'),(208731,2763,'report_intro','Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Phasellus massa erat, consectetur at semper at, feugiat vel orci. '),(208732,2763,'_report_intro','field_62f30eedb57e2'),(208733,2763,'report_link_url','#'),(208734,2763,'_report_link_url','field_62f30ef4b57e3'),(208735,2763,'report_link_text','Download'),(208736,2763,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(208737,2763,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(208738,2763,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(208739,2763,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(208740,2763,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(208741,2763,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(208742,2763,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(208743,2763,'problem_