t'),(212859,2788,'_report_title','field_62f30edfb57e1'),(212860,2788,'report_intro','Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Phasellus massa erat, consectetur at semper at, feugiat vel orci. '),(212861,2788,'_report_intro','field_62f30eedb57e2'),(212862,2788,'report_link_url','#'),(212863,2788,'_report_link_url','field_62f30ef4b57e3'),(212864,2788,'report_link_text','Download'),(212865,2788,'_report_link_text','field_62f30f01b57e4'),(212866,2788,'solutions_content','The housing system is complex, and no one solution will solve the complex problems we now face but there are some critical first steps to be taken now.\r\n<ul>\r\n 	<li>Set out an ambitious national housing agreement between commonwealth and state governments with targets and funding for the construction of affordable homes.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out tax breaks for property investors and using the increase in revenue to build more public housing.</li>\r\n 	<li>Establish laws which limit rental increases beyond what is fair.</li>\r\n 	<li>Rebalance tenancy laws to provide renters with more security and control, such as eliminating no grounds evictions.</li>\r\n 	<li>Phase out stamp duty and replace it with a broad-based land tax.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4>While there are many opinions on what policy changes will fix the housing market, doing nothing is not an option.</h4>'),(212867,2788,'_solutions_content','field_640e8b307a958'),(212868,2788,'problem_icons_0_prob_icon','1699'),(212869,2788,'_problem_icons_0_prob_icon','field_640fa0291d519'),(212870,2788,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','70% highly concerned'),(212871,2788,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerned_stat','field_640fa0dd81d95'),(212872,2788,'problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','are highly concerned'),(212873,2788,'_problem_icons_0_prob_concerded_text','field_640fa10181d96'),(212874,2788,'problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text',''),(212875,2788,'_problem_icons_0_prob_issue_text','field_640fa11a81d97'),(212876,2788,'problem_icons','4'),(21287